1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,900
Follow the literature review workflow.

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:11,900
Researchers define the scope and confirm conclusions.

3
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:17,900
Define the research questions and review scope.

4
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:24,900
Set inclusion and exclusion criteria.

5
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:31,900
Choose summary fields and contribution categories.

6
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:38,900
Decide which steps require human review.

7
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:46,900
Build search plans with concept groups and synonyms.

8
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:55,900
Inspect queries, year limits and database scope.

9
00:00:56,150 --> 00:01:05,900
Inspect database retrieval and import options.

10
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:11,900
Review screening decisions and category labels.

11
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:19,900
Read each title, abstract and decision rationale.

12
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:30,900
Check the evidence before confirming a decision.

13
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:38,900
Review a study with an original PDF and saved summary.

14
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:46,900
Read the original beside its summary and labels.

15
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:56,900
Check contributions, validation and supporting evidence.

16
00:01:57,150 --> 00:02:05,900
Read the summary alongside the corresponding source pages.

17
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:15,900
Human verification remains an explicit researcher action.

18
00:02:16,150 --> 00:02:23,900
Choose contribution labels and search-plan scope.

19
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:31,900
Set grouping instructions for a research perspective.

20
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:39,900
Use source-linked summaries to support synthesis.

21
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:45,900
Inspect recorded task status and progress.

22
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:51,900
Keep task history for follow-up and review.

23
00:02:52,150 --> 00:03:01,900
AI assists the workflow. Researchers own the conclusions.
